Here's a prioritized list of suggestions based on what the app currently has and what would provide the most value:

---
High Impact / Missing Core Features

1. Attendance Tracking
The schedule planner knows when classes happen, but there's no way to mark who actually showed up. A simple roll-call UI per session (present / absent / late) with a daily attendance summary on the dashboard would be very practical. You could also set thresholds — alert when a student misses more than X% of sessions.

2. Parent/Guardian Portal
Students can log in, but parents have no visibility. A read-only parent role with access to their child's grades, attendance, and assignment status would be very valuable for an afterschool context where parents are paying and want to stay informed.

3. Fee & Payment Tracking
No financial layer exists at all. A simple payments table (amount, date, method, notes) linked to students with a balance view and overdue alerts would make the app much more complete for administrative staff.

4. Bulk Student Import (CSV/Excel)
Enrollment is one-by-one right now. A CSV/Excel import with a preview step and duplicate detection would save huge amounts of time at the start of a semester.

---
Meaningful Enhancements to Existing Features

5. Dashboard Drill-Downs
The stat cards (total students, today's classes, etc.) are read-only. Making them clickable — e.g., clicking "Today's Classes" navigates to Schedule filtered to today — would make the dashboard actually useful as a navigation hub.

6. Student Progress Report (PDF)
The transcript export exists for grades, but a combined report per student (grades + attendance once that exists + assignment completion rate + teacher notes) would be the kind of document parents and students actually ask for. ClosedXML/PDF export is already wired in.

7. Assignment Grading
Assignments track submissions but teachers can't grade them within the app. A simple grade/feedback field on each submission (linked back to the Grades systemn assignments and grades.

